continue to the next dependent experiment.

IF RESULT IS NEGATIVE:
document the failure and identify which assumption failed.

IF RESULT IS PARTIAL:
refine only the failed mechanism.

IF RESULT IS INCONCLUSIVE:
design a discriminating experiment.

IF RESULT IS ALREADY EXPLAINED BY THE MODEL:
classify it as a prerequisite rather than a discovery.

IF AN UNEXPECTED PHENOMENON APPEARS:
pause the planned sequence and investigate it.

The research tree must therefore be result-driven.

